WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.027 --> 00:00:00.960
(light orchestral music)

00:00:00.960 --> 00:00:02.030
- [Jayna] In the ballet world,

00:00:02.030 --> 00:00:03.840
there are two types of dancers:

00:00:03.840 --> 00:00:06.320
You have a male dancer
and a female dancer.

00:00:06.320 --> 00:00:08.530
There's really no in between.

00:00:08.530 --> 00:00:12.283
Growing up, I really
didn't fit that binary,

00:00:14.580 --> 00:00:17.083
but I really do know who I am today.

00:00:17.950 --> 00:00:19.350
I'm a transgender ballerina.

00:00:24.550 --> 00:00:26.540
- [Announcer] This Great
Big Story was made possible

00:00:26.540 --> 00:00:27.793
by Procter &amp; Gamble.

00:00:29.663 --> 00:00:33.246
(rousing orchestral music)

00:00:38.120 --> 00:00:43.120
- [Jayna] I was born a male,
but I have always known

00:00:43.480 --> 00:00:45.190
that I've been gender-fluid.

00:00:45.190 --> 00:00:49.360
In my head and in my
heart, I really did feel

00:00:49.360 --> 00:00:52.682
that I was female, and
it's something everyone

00:00:52.682 --> 00:00:54.563
that I've met has known.

00:00:57.390 --> 00:00:59.410
- Oh, look!

00:00:59.410 --> 00:01:00.703
Nine-year-old Jay.

00:01:01.570 --> 00:01:04.630
Aw, so little.

00:01:04.630 --> 00:01:08.550
- I have been dancing
as a male since I was 5,

00:01:08.550 --> 00:01:12.410
but I was never able to
really express myself fully.

00:01:12.410 --> 00:01:14.480
As a male dancer, you have to be able

00:01:14.480 --> 00:01:16.120
to do a lot of partnering.

00:01:16.120 --> 00:01:18.480
It was really hard for me to pick up,

00:01:18.480 --> 00:01:21.793
and I just felt more that a
girl was partnering a girl.

00:01:23.670 --> 00:01:27.123
There really was no right
place for me to fit in.

00:01:30.320 --> 00:01:35.310
When I was alone, I danced
how I wanted to dance.

00:01:35.310 --> 00:01:39.080
I was just able to be
free for a few hours,

00:01:39.080 --> 00:01:42.971
and be able to just
express myself how I wanted

00:01:42.971 --> 00:01:44.471
to express myself.

00:01:47.057 --> 00:01:49.640
(somber music)

00:01:50.631 --> 00:01:55.440
When I was 17, I was in a
pre-professional program

00:01:55.440 --> 00:02:00.440
at a school; and when I decided
to come out to the school,

00:02:00.490 --> 00:02:04.868
the school was not as
accepting as my parents and I

00:02:04.868 --> 00:02:06.733
thought it was going to be.

00:02:09.110 --> 00:02:11.940
At the end of the school
year, they told me

00:02:11.940 --> 00:02:16.940
that they did not want me
to come back as a female,

00:02:18.890 --> 00:02:21.110
and they were not going to extend

00:02:21.110 --> 00:02:24.060
my scholarship as a female.

00:02:24.060 --> 00:02:27.170
I sort of gave up trying to
prove myself to the school

00:02:27.170 --> 00:02:30.110
because I really would rather be somewhere

00:02:30.110 --> 00:02:31.563
where I feel wanted.

00:02:32.532 --> 00:02:35.900
(rousing orchestral music)

00:02:35.900 --> 00:02:40.570
(instructor speaking foreign language)

00:02:40.570 --> 00:02:44.980
After the school year ended,
I went back to home to train

00:02:44.980 --> 00:02:49.150
with my current dance studio,
First State Dance Academy,

00:02:49.150 --> 00:02:52.615
as my true self, as a
female; and dancing there

00:02:52.615 --> 00:02:55.557
makes me feel very supported.

00:02:55.557 --> 00:02:57.320
- [Instructor] Nice, good.

00:02:57.320 --> 00:02:59.930
- [Jayna] And I'm in a class
where I can just dance,

00:02:59.930 --> 00:03:02.673
and not have to worry
about the outside world.

00:03:04.769 --> 00:03:05.602
- [Instructor] Stay.

00:03:05.602 --> 00:03:06.435
- Whoo!

00:03:06.435 --> 00:03:08.043
Yay!
(group applauding)

00:03:08.043 --> 00:03:10.555
Ring the bell!
(bell ringing)

00:03:10.555 --> 00:03:12.558
(group laughing)

00:03:12.558 --> 00:03:14.784
- [Jayna] There aren't
really many differences

00:03:14.784 --> 00:03:18.470
when it comes to male and female training.

00:03:18.470 --> 00:03:21.730
We go through barre, center, jumps, turns.

00:03:21.730 --> 00:03:22.583
It's just as a male dancer,

00:03:22.583 --> 00:03:24.613
you tend to jump a little bit more,

00:03:24.613 --> 00:03:27.630
whereas females do pointe work.

00:03:27.630 --> 00:03:29.010
- [Instructor] Six and seven.

00:03:29.010 --> 00:03:30.430
- [Jayna] I think the most difficult part

00:03:30.430 --> 00:03:33.070
of dancing on pointe is everything.

00:03:33.070 --> 00:03:36.250
You're basically standing
on top of your toes

00:03:36.250 --> 00:03:37.713
in these hard shoes.

00:03:38.840 --> 00:03:39.955
- Put weight on your back foot,

00:03:39.955 --> 00:03:43.290
so you can move your
front foot. (laughing)

00:03:43.290 --> 00:03:45.380
- [Jayna] I really was surprised to see

00:03:45.380 --> 00:03:48.868
that pointe wasn't as easy and graceful

00:03:48.868 --> 00:03:53.390
as the other girls made it,
but the more that I did it

00:03:53.390 --> 00:03:56.134
throughout the week, in
classes and rehearsals,

00:03:56.134 --> 00:03:59.490
the more that my feet
started to mold to my shoes.

00:03:59.490 --> 00:04:01.283
- There you go, good job.

00:04:05.080 --> 00:04:07.110
- [Jayna] After a month
of training on pointe,

00:04:07.110 --> 00:04:10.410
my dance teacher cast me as a snow queen

00:04:10.410 --> 00:04:13.090
in her production of "The Nutcracker".

00:04:13.090 --> 00:04:16.400
It was nerveracking,
because it was my first role

00:04:16.400 --> 00:04:17.520
as a female.

00:04:17.520 --> 00:04:22.520
I was shocked at the fact
that I didn't mess up at all,

00:04:22.700 --> 00:04:26.050
but I was more excited to just perform

00:04:26.050 --> 00:04:27.369
in front of an audience.

00:04:27.369 --> 00:04:28.600
(audience cheering)
(audience applauding)

00:04:28.600 --> 00:04:32.270
At the end of the day, I
really am just a ballerina.

00:04:32.270 --> 00:04:35.750
My goal is to dance professionally.

00:04:35.750 --> 00:04:37.970
I'm just like the other girls.

00:04:37.970 --> 00:04:41.770
I am working hard, and
I am striving to get

00:04:41.770 --> 00:04:42.846
to where I wanna be.

00:04:42.846 --> 00:04:47.013
("Dance of the Sugar Plum Fairy")

00:04:49.688 --> 00:04:53.105
(light electronic music)

